1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,162
Esports World Cup 2026 Brings $75 Million Prize Pool to Paris.

2
00:00:06,112 --> 00:00:18,937
The Esports World Cup 2026 descended upon Paris this July, transforming the city into a global gaming hub with a record $75 million prize pool across 25 competitive titles.

3
00:00:18,937 --> 00:00:30,537
The month-long festival, held at the Paris Expo Porte de Versailles, attracted over 180,000 live attendees and a concurrent online audience of 114 million viewers.

4
00:00:30,537 --> 00:00:40,762
Marquee events included the League of Legends World Cup, Counter-Strike 2's international championship, and the Valorant World Tour finals, each drawing massive crowds.

5
00:00:40,762 --> 00:00:54,387
Saudi Arabia's Esports World Cup Foundation, which launched the event in 2024, expanded the Paris edition to include an open esports festival with live music, developer panels, and amateur tournaments.

6
00:00:54,387 --> 00:01:01,875
France's deep esports culture and central European location made Paris a natural choice for the 2026 edition.

7
00:01:01,875 --> 00:01:13,625
The event featured a new Club Championship format where organizations earned points across multiple game titles, with Team Liquid claiming the $10 million grand prize for overall club excellence.

8
00:01:13,625 --> 00:01:21,612
The EWC's rapid growth reflects the mainstreaming of competitive gaming as a legitimate spectator sport on the global stage.

